.TH "GF-SIGNED-IN-USER-UPDATE-USER-PREFERENCES" "1" "May 2026" "" ""

.SH NAME
gf-signed-in-user-update-user-preferences - Updates user preferences


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgf signed-in-user update-user-preferences [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Updates user preferences

.PP
Omitting a key (\fBtheme\fR, \fBhomeDashboardUID\fR, \fBtimezone\fR) will cause the current value to be replaced with the system default value.

.PP
Body schema (UpdatePrefsCmd):
  cookies               array
  homeDashboardId       number         The numerical :id of a favorited dashboard
  homeDashboardUID      string
  language              string
  navbar                object
  navbar.bookmarkUrls   array
  queryHistory          object
  queryHistory.homeTab  string
  regionalFormat        string
  theme                 string         enum: light | dark | system
  timezone              string         enum: utc | browser
  weekStart             string

.PP
Response schema (UpdateUserPreferencesOK.Payload):
  message  string


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--body\fP=""
	Request body JSON or path to a JSON file (e.g. --body=/path/to/body.json, --body='{"foo": "bar"}'). The 'Body schema' block above lists fields and types; use --describe-body-jsonschema for a strict JSON Schema.

